 "intro": {
  "text": "A fork is one piece attacking two enemy pieces at once. Every piece can fork, even a pawn, but knights are famous for it: the forked pieces cannot block a knight's attack or hit back at it, unless one of them is a knight too. A fork that comes with check is the most powerful kind, because the king must move and the other piece is lost. Not every fork wins material, though: check how your opponent could escape before you play it.",
  "credit": {
   "source": "Wikibooks, Chess/Tactics",
   "url": "https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Chess/Tactics",
   "licence": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
   "licenceUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
   "authors": "Wikibooks contributors (see the page history)"
  }
 },
